// Witness for rule J1: a property whose body is a member access that does NOT correspond to it.
//
// This is the permuted-constructor defeat, one screen further down the same predicate. Case 2 was
// narrowed to require that a constructor assign each parameter to the member CORRESPONDING to it,
// and case 1 went on accepting any member access at all - so exchanging two ceilings inside a
// constructor became relevant while publishing the wrong one from a property stayed exempt, which
// is the same edit with the same effect on every bounded read.
//
// MaxSectionCount publishes the declared-count ceiling. It must be relevant, and so must the
// accessor form of it below. MaxDeclaredCount and Depth are the accepting direction: each returns
// the field that corresponds to it and stays exempt, so the clause is a correspondence check and
// not a rule that ends exemption case 1.

namespace Probe;

